course: dictionary
lesson: 2598
title: Depend: changing or trusting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word depend has two main meanings. The first is to change according to something. «Your dose depends on your age and weight» means the right amount for you changes when your age or weight changes. The second is to need someone or trust them. Babies depend on their parents.
explain: When you see depends on or depending on, ask yourself: what does this change with? «Clubs are for fun and learning, so the best choice depends on what the child enjoys» tells you the best club changes with what the child enjoys, not with what other families do.
explain: «You can depend on me» does not mean you lean on me. It means you can trust me to be there when you need me. Check the words around depend: they will tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Depend is a verb: depend, depends, depended, depending.
fact: «Depends on» means changes according to something, as in «the answer depends on the numbers».
fact: «Depending on» is often followed by the thing that changes the answer, as in «depending on whether» some countries are counted.
fact: «You can depend on me» means you can trust me.
fact: Babies depend on their parents, which means they need them to be looked after.
exercise: «Your dose depends on your age and weight.» What does depends on mean here? | Is always safe to share | *Changes according to your age and weight | Is decided by your sister | Is the same for everyone
exercise: Ella says, «You can depend on me.» What does it mean? | You might not come, so do not wait for me | *You can trust me to be there | I need you to help me carry my bag | I like the bus more than walking
exercise: «Europe has about 44 to 50 countries, depending on whether partly European countries are counted.» Which word shows that the number can change? | Europe | *depending | countries | about
test: «Babies depend on their parents.» What does this mean? | *They need their parents to look after them | They never need any help | They are always bigger than their parents | They go to school alone
test: Ravi says, «It depends.» What does he mean? | The answer is always the same | *The answer is not always the same and changes | He has a secret | He has made a rule
exam: Which meaning of depend fits «babies depend on their parents»? | To grow bigger each year | To count and add up numbers | To change according to something | *To need someone and rely on them
